WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.150
- I know I'm supposed to be like,

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.320
I'm supposed to be like a
talk show host right now,

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.487
but like I'm also a singer and like,

00:00:06.487 --> 00:00:07.550
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.118
like you're incredible,

00:00:10.118 --> 00:00:10.951
- Thank you

00:00:10.951 --> 00:00:11.784
- Like you literally are.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.340
So thank you for letting
me sing with you earlier.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.173
- Oh yeah

00:00:16.173 --> 00:00:17.050
- It's literally a dream come true.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.060
Like no lie.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.700
I love you so much, but I have to ask

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.783
I'm just curious with a voice like yours,

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.500
like were people just like, oh my God.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.000
Like from like childhood with you,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.480
like do you remember
the first time you sang?

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.150
And like.
- Well.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.650
- People were floored?

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.900
- My family was super musical.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.733
- [Kelly] Oh
- We had all these aunts

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:39.160
- and uncles and everything
who always loved to play,

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.450
like get together and play the ukuleles

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.340
and sing the old songs and stuff.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:47.880
And so it was pretty easy
just to go from that to

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.220
to being asked to sing at one of

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.680
my parents' cocktail parties.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.619
- It was like fluid. Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:51.619 --> 00:00:52.580
You're really used to it. Yeah

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:53.730
- It wasn't much of a stretch really.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.563
- Yeah.

00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:55.560
- And as a little kid, you know,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.750
little kids love to show off in front of

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:58.583
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- The grown ups, you know.

00:00:58.583 --> 00:00:59.416
- [Kelly] Yeah. Look at me.

00:00:59.416 --> 00:01:01.275
- Yeah. Well, yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:02.108
Yeah. I'm funny right.

00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:02.941
- Yeah
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:02.941 --> 00:01:04.820
- And so I used to do this,

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.190
I think from early age like six to eight,

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:09.620
I was doing this rendition

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.619
of the Hawaiian Wedding
Song as Ethel Merman.

00:01:12.619 --> 00:01:13.452
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:13.452 --> 00:01:15.640
So it was like a child, you know?

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.500
So I think that's, that's
where I got the sort of

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.710
feeling that singing
and acting go together.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.750
- Yeah, oh, I do agree with that.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.500
Like while I'm singing, are you like this?

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.770
Because I hate acting, but I love,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.880
I feel like I do it on stage

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.350
cause you jump into character of wherever

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:31.409
you were when you wrote the song.

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:32.242
- Right, yeah, yeah.

00:01:32.242 --> 00:01:33.540
Is that ever hard for you,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.710
depending upon the song?

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.543
Like, you know, like.

00:01:35.543 --> 00:01:37.900
- For me, it's not the
songs that are too intense.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:40.070
It's the ones that I've grown out of.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:40.903
- [Kelly] Ah

00:01:40.903 --> 00:01:42.800
- Like, you know I
don't wanna say anything

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:44.610
about too specific songs but

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.250
- You don't like poo poo
on the songs but yeah

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:47.860
- But a song like Magic Man, you know

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:48.693
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.693 --> 00:01:50.390
- Was written way back when I was

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:53.440
in my super early twenties
and with my first love and.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.986
- Don't you bash Magic
Man right now Ma'am,

00:01:54.986 --> 00:01:56.687
(audience laughs)

00:01:56.687 --> 00:01:57.520
- That's what I meant.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.700
- I will actually tackle you.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:01:59.690
- That's what I meant.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:00.523
I don't wanna bash any songs but...

00:02:00.523 --> 00:02:01.356
- You know why?

00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:02.540
I think it was actually
the first hard song

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:03.830
I ever heard as a child,

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:06.470
and I was like, and
honestly it was because

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:08.810
it was women and usually you always

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.820
heard men doing the rock stuff.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:11.900
And so I remember,

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.210
cause my brother's like a decade older,

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.670
and anything they were listening to

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.290
was always like men and
I was like, wait, what?

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.123
I can do this?

00:02:17.123 --> 00:02:18.760
And it was like representation
at its finest point.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.000
I was like, wait, women
are able to do this too.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.980
And it was really cool cause

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.200
I feel like y'all opened the door

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.650
for all the, for the Alanis Morrisettes

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.276
for all these women in music later on.

00:02:27.276 --> 00:02:28.109
(Audience claps)

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:32.720
And, and I, I mean, I often do wonder

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.510
like back in the day,
was that really hard?

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:36.412
Like being the only

00:02:36.412 --> 00:02:37.245
- [Ann] Yeah

00:02:37.245 --> 00:02:38.160
was there just so much,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.190
was it just just oozing in misogyny?

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.097
Like was it just?

00:02:41.097 --> 00:02:42.710
(Ann laughs)

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.330
- I like that oozing in misogyny.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.163
Yes. It was.

00:02:45.163 --> 00:02:46.270
- It happens, We've all been in that room.

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:48.280
- It was total immersion.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.210
- Immersion.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:54.210
- Yeah. But, yeah, back
when I started out it was,

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.070
it was all radio right?

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:56.903
- Yeah.

00:02:56.903 --> 00:02:58.472
- Like there was no Spotify
or anything like that

00:02:58.472 --> 00:02:59.305
- No streaming services

00:02:59.305 --> 00:03:00.138
- It was just all radio.

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:00.971
- Yeah.

00:03:00.971 --> 00:03:03.890
- And so radio had this
kind of unspoken rule

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:07.650
that they could only play
one female artist per hour.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.370
So if you weren't like
Joan Baez, a folk singer

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.470
or if you weren't a disco diva,

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:14.500
you were just outta luck.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.350
- There was no room.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:16.183
- Right.

00:03:16.183 --> 00:03:17.016
- At the table. Oh.

00:03:17.016 --> 00:03:18.910
- So when we did manage to get a

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.740
Heart song or two played on the radio,

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.370
it was kind of a revelation.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.546
- [Kelly] Yeah. I mean what a perfect one.

00:03:26.546 --> 00:03:29.040
So is it true, I didn't
actually know this,

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.060
like growing up, singing Barracuda.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.320
I didn't know it was about sexism,

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.480
but that's true right?

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.360
- Yeah. Yep. Yep.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:34.193
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:03:34.193 --> 00:03:35.026
- Yeah

00:03:35.026 --> 00:03:36.190
- I love when people write songs though.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.023
and like when you're young,

00:03:37.023 --> 00:03:37.856
you don't know like whatever

00:03:37.856 --> 00:03:39.210
and you have this whole other idea

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.210
and then you're like, oh, it's way off.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.000
- [Ann] So that's how it is, yeah.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:43.833
- Yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:46.370
- I was really, I was really surprised.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.960
Like I was so naive and I just thought,

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.190
well we're bringing
our word to the people.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.980
You know, it was almost like spiritual.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:53.813
- Yeah.

00:03:53.813 --> 00:03:54.646
- And then I get into this room

00:03:54.646 --> 00:03:57.299
with these really sleazy,
you know, industry guys,

00:03:57.299 --> 00:03:58.132
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:58.132 --> 00:03:58.965
who are saying all kinds of

00:03:58.965 --> 00:04:01.210
really disrespectful stuff, you know?

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:02.043
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:02.043 --> 00:04:03.380
- And it made me mad and I went back

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.439
to the hotel and wrote
the words to Barracuda.

00:04:05.439 --> 00:04:06.272
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:06.272 --> 00:04:08.260
- And it made me feel better, you know?

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.310
- Do you feel like it has changed though,

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.230
like dramatically since the, you know,

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.440
when Heart first broke?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.450
- Yes, I do.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.860
I think it's changed in a lot of ways.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.430
You don't have to dress up in a

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.790
French maid outfit and
be the centerfold now.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:21.623
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:21.623 --> 00:04:22.456
- When you're really a musician, you know?

00:04:22.456 --> 00:04:23.289
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:23.289 --> 00:04:26.310
- But some of the old
stuff is still in place.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.480
It's just gone underground.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.520
It's just.
- [Kelly] Sneaky

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.910
- Deep and systemic, you know?

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.937
- Yeah.

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:34.860
- And that's, lots of
progress has been made

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.810
in terms of women having their respect

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.830
and being real and everything.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.216
- And like more than one played an hour.

00:04:40.216 --> 00:04:41.049
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:41.049 --> 00:04:41.882
- Right?
- Yeah

00:04:41.882 --> 00:04:42.900
But, but there still is

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.860
a lot more room for improvement.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.280
- Yeah. Agreed. Agree,
in all aspects of life.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.500
So your new album,

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.730
- it's called Fierce Bliss.
- [Ann] Yes.

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.350
Which is a rad title.
- [Ann] Thank you.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.845
So it was inspired by a road trip?

00:04:53.845 --> 00:04:54.678
(Audience claps)

00:04:54.678 --> 00:04:55.540
- [Ann] Yeah, thank you.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.194
- I love a road trip.

00:04:57.194 --> 00:04:58.810
- Woo.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.250
Yes. My husband and I
love to take road trips.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.083
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:02.083 --> 00:05:05.080
- And it was 2020, it was in the midst

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.705
of the height of the pandemic, right.

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:07.538
- Yeah

00:05:07.538 --> 00:05:09.170
And we'd already been in the house

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.350
for six or eight months and we just went

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:13.610
can no do, can no do this no more.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.443
- [Kelly] We have to move, yeah.

00:05:14.443 --> 00:05:16.800
- And so we, we leased a tour bus

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.062
and we live in Florida now.

00:05:19.062 --> 00:05:19.895
- Yeah.

00:05:19.895 --> 00:05:21.740
- But we drove out to the west coast.

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:22.800
Then we went up to Seattle.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.992
Then we went to San Francisco

00:05:23.992 --> 00:05:25.530
and then we went to LA
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.470
- And all the national parks in between.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:28.640
- Beautiful.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.570
So did being on that road
trip, is that kind of,

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:32.930
what I guess, led you to do Fierce Bliss?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:33.840
Like inspired you?

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.434
- Yeah. It gave me a lot of fresh,

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:41.130
you know, input oF the beauty

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:44.610
and just, it energized
me and it was peaceful.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:47.440
So that's what it takes for
me to write is I need peace

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.140
and I need room to daydream
and quiet, you know?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:51.973
- [Kelly] Oh I know.

00:05:51.973 --> 00:05:52.806
- and the tour life is not that

00:05:52.806 --> 00:05:53.639
- Yeah.

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:54.472
- the tour life, as you know, is

00:05:54.472 --> 00:05:55.305
- It's chaotic

00:05:55.305 --> 00:05:57.016
- It's like a crossroads
of just all these different

00:05:57.016 --> 00:05:57.849
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:57.849 --> 00:05:59.010
- People's energies and everything.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:01.164
You have to be just focused on that one

00:06:01.164 --> 00:06:04.050
two hours you're gonna do on stage.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:04.883
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:04.883 --> 00:06:06.800
- Yeah. So the road trip
really helped me write.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:07.860
- I love that.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.650
So next year is the 50th
anniversary of Heart.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:11.517
- Yeah.

00:06:11.517 --> 00:06:12.350
(Audience claps)

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:13.990
- So that's amazing.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:16.160
So do you have to any plans to celebrate?

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:17.810
I mean that's awesome. 50 years.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:18.843
- We do.

00:06:18.843 --> 00:06:19.676
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:19.676 --> 00:06:21.440
- But I gotta say it's too early days

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.140
for me to talk about it now.

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:23.973
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:23.973 --> 00:06:24.947
- I'm not at liberty to discuss it.

00:06:24.947 --> 00:06:25.940
- Ooh I like it.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:26.903
- But

00:06:26.903 --> 00:06:27.736
(Ann laughs)

00:06:27.736 --> 00:06:28.569
- Yeah, that makes it tease

00:06:28.569 --> 00:06:29.402
- But yeah.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:06:29.402 --> 00:06:30.540
- Yeah. We are gonna do a thing.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.951
- Okay. Just asking for a friend.

00:06:31.951 --> 00:06:33.730
(Both laugh)

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:36.270
Ann's new album is called Fierce Bliss.

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:38.530
It's out now and Ann is performing

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.620
for us later in the show.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.093
You will definitely wanna
stick around for that.

